    "ruleType": "unit-ability",
    "group": "Commissar Yarrick",
    "summary": "As your opponent's [Movement phase](vsdata:core-rule/movement-phase) ends, you can pick 2 units, measuring from this model:\n\n- 1 enemy unit that ended a move, or was set up, within 8\"\n- 1 **REGIMENT** unit of yours within 6\" that this model can see and that, this phase, has neither made a **[Normal move](vsdata:core-rule/normal-move)** nor been the target of the **[Fire Overwatch](vsdata:ability/core.fire-overwatch)** Stratagem\n\nYour **REGIMENT** unit can then do 1 of these:\n\n- Move up to D6\" as a Normal move.\n- Shoot, targeting only the picked enemy unit, which must be an eligible target. For the rest of the phase, its ranged attacks need an unmodified 6 to hit, regardless of modifiers or the weapon's Ballistic Skill.\n- Declare a charge. Its **[charge move](vsdata:core-rule/charge-move)** must end **engaged** with the picked enemy unit, and even a successful charge gives it no Charge bonus this turn.",
